Comment:

// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the initial size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the old element at this index was null, or equal to the old element at this index.

We are in method add(int index, Object element) overriding ArrayList.add. The method inserts element at given index, shifting subsequent elements to the right.

We need assert statement describing postcondition.

Premise: index between 0 and initial size inclusive. Initial size = old size before addition. So condition: 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()).

Then conclusion: for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position (i+1?) is either null if the old element at this index was null, or equal to the old element at this index.

Interpretation: After insertion, elements from index to oldSize-1 shift right by one. So for each i in [index, oldSize-1] (i valid old index), after operation, element at position i+1 equals old element at i (or null if old element at i was null). Since equality with null is just equality.

Thus we assert: (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));

But need to account for null case: "either null if the old element at this index was null, or equal to the old element at this index." That's exactly equality (null equals null). So just equality works.

But note that this.get returns Role, but list holds Object. But we can use this.get(i+1).equals? Since could be null. Use == for reference equality? In spec they often use .equals for non-null. Use (\old(this.get(i)) == null ? this.get(i+1) == null : this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)))).

Simplify: this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i)) (reference equality) works for null and objects. Use ==.

Thus final assert:

assert (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));

