Interpretation: pre-state size = oldSize = \old(this.size()). Index is between 0 and oldSize inclusive (since insertion at end allowed). For each i such that index <= i < oldSize, after insertion, the element at position i+1 (next position) is either null if old element at i was null, else equal to old element at i.

We need to refer to element at position after insertion: this.get(i+1). Since after insertion, list size = oldSize+1.

We need to use \old(this.get(i)) maybe. But need to be careful: get returns Role, but list holds Object; but we can still refer.

So assert: (index >=0 && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i+1) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)))).

